1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Snorri "Gode" Þorgrímson=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Snorre Gode, Snorre Prest, Snorre the Priest - religious and community leader on Iceland around the year 1000.
2 CONT * Father: Thorgrim Gode (killed shortly before Snorre's birth)
2 CONT * Mother: Tordis Sursdotter
2 CONT * Birth: ca 954 (Snorre Godes Liv says he died in his 77th year)
2 CONT * Death: 1031 (the year after Olav Haraldsson's death - chapter 65)
2 CONT * The major source for his life is "Eyrbyggja Saga"; he also features prominently in "Njåls Saga" and "Laxdøla Saga". The short "Snorre Godes Liv" gives the sequence of his children and their mothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Asdis,''' daugher of Styr (from chapter 28 of Eyrbyggja Saga)
2 CONT * '''Turidar,''' daughter of Illuga the Red
2 CONT * '''Hallfrid Einarsdotter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorre had many children. According to "Snorre Godes Liv", he had 3 wives, giving him 19 free-born children, and 3 listed children with thralls.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Asdis:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * First, Thórðr chose it was ellstr
2 CONT * second,  Thorodd
2 CONT * third,  Thorsteinn
2 CONT * fourth, Guðlaugr munkr.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with , Thurid Illugadotter Illuga ins rauða=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fifth  Sigríðr,
2 CONT * Sixth, Audur Unn 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Hallfríðar Einarsdóttur=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Seventh,  Sjaundi Kleppr,
2 CONT * Eighth Halldora,
2 CONT * Ninth Thordis,
2 CONT * tenth Guðrún,
2 CONT * 11th Halldórr,
2 CONT * twelfth Máni,
2 CONT * thirteenth Eyjolf,
2 CONT * Fourteenth Thora,
2 CONT * fifteenth,  Hallbera,
2 CONT * Sixteenth Thurid,
2 CONT * seventeenth Thorleifr,
2 CONT * eighteenth year, Aalov
2 CONT * nineteenth Snorri. He was born after his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with thralls:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Thórðr chose,
2 CONT * Jörundr
2 CONT * Thorhildr
2 CONT
2 CONT The list from chapter 65 of Eyrbyggja Saga seems to skip some, listing only 14 children, and list them by significance rather than order of birth (numbers from above):
2 CONT
2 CONT =Daughters:=
2 CONT
2 CONT ** Sigrid, married to Brand Vermundsson and Kolle Tormodsson (5)
2 CONT ** Audur Unn, married to Viga-Barde, later to Sigurd, son of Tore Hund in Norway (6)
2 CONT ** Tordis, married to Bolle Bolleson, ancestor of the Gilsbekk clan (9)
2 CONT ** Halbera, marreid to Tord, son of Sturla Tjodreksson (15)
2 CONT ** Tora, married to Keru-Berse, son of Halldor Olavsson, later to Torgrim svide (14)
2 CONT ** Turid, married to Gunnlaug, son of Steintor (16)
2 CONT ** Gudrun, married to Kalv på Solheimar (10)
2 CONT ** Halldora, married to Torgeir from Aasgardsholar (8)
2 CONT ** Aalov, married to Jørund Torfinsson (18)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sons (same chapter):=
2 CONT
2 CONT ** Halldor, ancestor of Sturlungane and Vatsfjordingane (11)
2 CONT ** Torodd, who lived on Saakonefjell (2)
2 CONT ** Maane, who lived on Saudafjell, father of Ljot (12)
2 CONT ** Torstein, who lived at Laugarbrekka (3)
2 CONT ** Tord Kause, who lived in Dufgusdal (1)
2 CONT ** Øyjolv, who lived in Lambestad (13)
2 CONT ** Torleiv, who lived in Medalfjellsstrand, ancestor of the Ballæringarne clan (17)
2 CONT ** Snorre, who lived in Sælingsdalstunga after his father (19)
2 CONT ** Klepp, whose fate and descendants are unknown (7)
2 CONT
2 CONT =[http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landnamabogen History]
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorri Þorgrímsson or Snorri Goði (Icelandic pronunciation; 963-1031[1]) was a prominent chieftain in Western Iceland, who featured in a number of Icelandic sagas. The main source of his life is the Eyrbyggja saga, in which he is 
2 CONC the main character, although he also figures prominently in Njál's saga and the Laxdæla saga. Snorri was the nephew of Gísli Súrsson, the hero of Gísla saga, while his son Halldórr was the subject of two tales detailing Halldórr's
2 CONC  service in the retinue of the Norwegian king Haraldr Sigurðarson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eyrbyggja Saga says of him "He was a very shrewd man with unusual foresight, a long memory and a taste for vengeance. To his friends he gave good counsel, but his enemies learned to fear the advice he gave."[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Njál's saga says of him "Snorri was reckoned the wisest man in Iceland, not counting those who were prescient
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorri góði Þorgrímsson Tilnavn / fordanskning: Snorre Gode Lokalitet: Helgafell, vestl. IslandRelationer: Efterkommer af Thorolf Mostarskæg. Søn af Gisle Sursons søster Thordis og Thorgrim Thorsteinsson. Fader til Thorstein, Halb
2 CONC era, Thurid den Kloge, Halldor Kilder: Islændingebogen: 1; Landnamabogen: 63, S75, S79, 69, 72, 73, 74, S100, S109, 96, 110, 112, 152 Noter: Den store høvding, som kendes fra flere af sagaerne.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
