1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ranveig / Ragnhild Sigurdsdatter Hund=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Estate owner wife at Bjarkøygods, Bjarkøy, Harstad'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * She was the daughter of Sigurd Thoreson Hund at Bjarkøy and Aud Snorresdotter
2 CONT * Birth:	1035 in Bjarkøy, Harstad, Troms, Norway
2 CONT * Death:	1080 (45) in Bjarkøy, Harstad, Troms, Norway
2 CONT * BJARKOY is a Norwegian høvdingætt in Hålogaland and of no man's family from the Middle Ages which had its headquarters in Bjarkøy in Troms , but eventually had extensive lands in several places in Norway. The genus is often divi
2 CONC ded into older and younger.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://no.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bjark%C3%B8y%C3%A6tten The Bjarkøy Family, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT The oldest part is known Tore from Bjarkøy , who during a visit to his foster sister Sigrid (Storråde) was burned in together with Harald Grenske , father of Olav Haraldsson . Tore's sons were Sigurd Toresson on Trondenes , just s
2 CONC outh of Bjarkøy, and Tore Hund on Bjarkøy who helped lead the rebellion against King Olav Haraldsson and personally helped to kill the king in the battle of Stiklestad in 1030 . Sigurd's son Asbjørn Selsbane was killed by the king
2 CONC 's men, but Tore Hund's son, Sigurd Toresson from Bjarkøy , had no son, but a daughter,Ragnhild Sigurdsdatter , who was married to Giskeætten by Jon Arnesson from Giske , son of Arne Arnesson . Jon is descended from Erling Skjalgs
2 CONC son at Sola and Astrid Tryggvesdatter , sister of King Olav Tryggvason . Ragnhild and Jon got their son Vidkun Jonsson from Bjarkøy who participated in King Magnus Berrføtt's army in Ireland. Sigurd Jorsalfares son Magnus was rais
2 CONC ed at Vidkun in Bjarkøy. -
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Jon Arnesson Giske,''' son of Arne Arnesson Giske and Gjertrud Erlingsdatter på Sola 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Vidkunn Jonsson,''' born about 1066, died after 1138. Was the foster father of Magnus Blinde.
2 CONT *''' Erling Jonsson, av Bjarkøy;''' birth: circa 1068 in Bjarkøy, Harstad, Troms, Norway
2 CONT *''' Gjertrud Jonsdatter Giske Bjarkøy;''' birth: circa 1070 in Bjarkøy, Troms, Norway
2 CONT * '''Sigurd Hund;''' Lyst Peaceless by King Magnus Barfot. Without known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT  '''Source:''' by Bjørn Jonson Dale in Yearbook for Sunnmøre 2016
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://no.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigurd_Toresson_fra_Bjarkøy Sigurd Toresson fra Bjarkøy, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigurd himself married a peer woman from Iceland, Aud Snorresdatter. She was the daughter of Snorre Gode, a man with a position in Iceland, and who actually called Torgrim Torgrimsson, and is mentioned in Eyrbyggja saga (Sagaen ab
2 CONC out Øyrbyggjaene) and in Njåls saga. Sigurd met Aud in Norway, but perhaps he knew her before. Aud was first married to a Viga-Barde (Viga = Drap) from Iceland who went with Aud to Norway. After a fierce quarrel, Viga-Barde left A
2 CONC ud and Miklagard, went into the guard corps and was later killed in a battle.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''With Aud, Sigurd had his daughter Ragnhild Sigurdsdatter who was strategically married to Jon Arnesson from Giske, son of Arne Arnesson, and he descended from Erling Skjalgsson at Sola and Astrid Tryggvesdatter, sister of Olav 
2 CONC Tryggvason. Ragnhild and Jon got their son Vidkun Jonsson from Bjarkøy, who is mentioned several times in the king's sagas.'''  Snorre Sturlasson also mentions that Ragnhild and Jon had Sigurd Hund, Erling Jonsson and Jartrud Jons
2 CONC datter.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://runeberg.org/nfaa/1107.html Project Runeberg]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) The Bjarkö family.  Like the Torberg brothers, Arne Arnesson was a faithful follower of Olof the Holy, despite the fact that he was also married to a daughter of Erling Skjalgsson.  When Olof returned to Norway, A. joined him a
2 CONC nd was severely wounded in the battle of Stiklastad. '''His son Jon married a daughter of Tore Hund and thereby inherited his ancestral estate Bjarkö. Jon's son was the well-known Vidkunn Jonsson from Magnus Barfot's last Irish tr
2 CONC ain (1103), whose son Erling during the mutual the wars belonged to Magnus Erlingsson's party.''' His son Vidkunn Erlingsson was killed at the age of 18 (1183) by Sverre's followers. With him the family died out and Bjarkö went th
2 CONC rough to his sister Ragnar's marriage to the lawyer in Hålogaland Bjarne Mardsson . From them descended the " 
2 CONT younger Bjarkö family", who later also inherited Giske. 
2 CONT
