3 TEXT In the latter days of the Viking occupation of Scotland and Ireland we know Thorstein the Red, grandson of Ketil Flatnose  was slain. Aud, mother of Thorstein and daughter of Ketil flatnose fled Ireland to the safety of Iceland, s
4 CONC topping in the isles to marry off her daughters. Aud captained the ship to Orkney Islands. One of the last viking strongholds and I believe where her father Ketil Flatnose was living having left the Hebrides under pressure of the 
4 CONC Scots. We know from the sagas Aud tried to talk her father Ketil into fleeing to Iceland with her but he refused.  Aud then captained the ship on its sail to the area of Breiðafjörður in Iceland leaving her father behind in Scotla
4 CONC nd. One ancient Viking settlement on Sanday island in the Orkney chain bears the name Kettletorf. An old Norse word meaning “The old abandoned home of Ketil.”
