1 OCCU Landnámsmaður í Saurbæ í Eyjafirði
1 TITL "Rotinn" (Rotten)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Landnámsmaður í Saurbæ í Eyjafirði.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogypage.tripod.com/landnama3.html (232)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Landnámu, his father was Eyjólfur Valgerðarson, son of Einar son of Auðun rotin Þórólfsson, a settler in Saurbæ in Eyjafjörður.
2 CONT
2 CONT Landnáma says that Auðun's father was Þórólf the one who brought Hrafna-Flók to Iceland and said, when he was asked to describe the country, that there drips butter from every straw; he was therefore called Þórólf mõgar. He is sai
2 CONC d to have been the son of Þorstein Skrofa, the son of Grím Kamban , who is said to have been the first to build the Faroe Islands .
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Helga, daughter of Helga magra, who gave them land inside Eyjafjörður, from Hálsi to Villingadal , and they lived in Saurbæ . Their children were Einar, father of Eyjólf Valgerðarson and grandfather of Guðmundar ríka an
2 CONC d Einar Þveræing , and Vigdís. After Auðun's death, Helga married Hámundi Heljarskinni , who had previously been married to her sister Ingunna, and their daughter was Yngvildur allrasystir, who married Örnólf son of Þórðar slítand
2 CONC a , a settler in Hörgárdal .
