2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Harald Hårfagre's Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "40. BIRTH OF HAKON THE GOOD.
2 CONT Earl Hakon Grjotgardson of Hlader had the whole rule over Throndhjem when King Harald was anywhere away in the country; and Hakon stood higher with the king than any in the country of Throndhjem. After Hakon's death his son Sigurd
2 CONC  succeeded to his power in Throndhjem, and was the earl, and had his mansion at Hlader. King Harald's sons, Halfdan the Black and Sigrod, who had been before in the house of his father Earl Hakon, continued to be brought up in his
2 CONC  house. The sons of Harald and Sigurd were about the same age. Earl Sigurd was one of the wisest men of his time, and married Bergljot, a daughter of Earl Thorer the Silent; and her mother was Alof Arbot, a daughter of Harald Harf
2 CONC ager. ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Erikssønnene kom til makten ca. 960. Sent på høsten 962 ble Sigurd overfalt på en lumsk måte av Harald Gråfeld og hans bror Erling og innebrent.
