1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ragnhild Erlingsdatter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Erling Ormsen "Skakke/ The Sharp" of Studla and Prinsesse av Norge Kristin Sigurdsdatter 
2 CONT * Ragnhild Erlingsdatter (born about 1150) was the daughter of Erling Skakke and Kristin Sigurdsdatter , daughter of Sigurd Jorsalfare . First married to Jon Torbergsson who fell in the battle of the Calfskin 1179 . Married again 
2 CONC to Halkjell Jonsson of Blindheimætten who fell in the Battle of Florvåg 1194 . [1] Grandmother of Magnus Lagabøte .
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWAY.htm#RagnhildErlingsdM1JThobergsM2Hallk'''elJons RAGNHILD Erlingsdatter.''']  Snorre names Ragnhild as "a daughter of princess Kristin and Earl Erling who was married to Jon Thorbergson of 
2 CONC Randaberg", recording that she "went away from the country with a man called Grim Rusle…to Constantinople where they were for a time and had some children"[526].  The Saga of King Sverre records the marriage of "Ragnhild daughter 
2 CONC of Earl Erling and Kristin Kings-daughter" and "Halkel son of Jon Hallkelsson"[527].  '''married firstly JON Thorbergsson from Randaberg''' (-killed in battle near Nidaros [Trondheim] 18 or 19 Jun 1179).  '''married secondly HALLK
2 CONC EL Jonsson''' from Blindheim Jarl in Norway, son of JON Hallkelsson & his wife Margrete of Norway [daughter of King Harald Gille] (-killed in battle Florevåg near Bergen 3 Apr 1194). -
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#AsulfSkulessonMThoraSkoptisd Project MedLands, Norway Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SKULI Tostesson Kongsfostre''' son of [TOSTIG Godwinsson & his wife Judith de Flandre] .  Snorre names "Skule, a son of Earl Toste, who since has been called the king's foster-son, and his brother Ketil Krok…of high family in E
2 CONC ngland" when recording that they accompanied Olav King of Norway after their father's were both killed at the battle of Stamford Bridge[222], the context suggesting that he and his brother were adults at the time.  If this is corr
2 CONC ect, they must have been their father's illegitimate sons and not the children of Tostig who were “unweaned” when their father died, referred to in the Vita Ædwardi Regis[223].  Morkinskinna records that “Skúli, the son of Jarl To
2 CONC stig Godwinson, and Ketill krókr from Hálogaland came to Norway with King Óláfr” after the failed invasion of England in 1066[224].  Snorre records that King Olav granted lands "eastward at Konungahella, Oslo, Tunsberg, Sarpsborg,
2 CONC  Bergen, and north at Nidaros" to Skule[225].  Morkinskinna records that “not long after King Haraldr´s fall Skúli went west to England to ask for the return of King Haraldr´s body” which was “readily granted to him”[226]. married
2 CONC  '''GUDRUN Nefsteinsdatter, daughter of NEFSTEIN --- & his wife Ingerid Sigurdsdatter.''' Snorre records that King Olav gave Skule "his female relative, Gudrun, the daughter of Nefstein…and Ingerid" in marriage[227].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Skule Tostesson "Kongsfostre"& his wife Gudrun had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''ASULF Skulesson of Rein'''   Snorre names "Asolf of Reine" as the son of Skule & his wife[228].  Morkinskinna names “Ásólfr, the father of Guthormr at Rein” as the son of “Skúli, the son of Jarl Tostig Godwinson”[2
2 CONC 29].  '''married THORA Skoptisdotter, daughter of SKOPTI Ogmundsson of Giske & his wife.'''  Snorre names "Thora, a daughter of Skopte Ogmundson" as the wife of "Asolf of Reine"[230]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2.         '''RAGNHILD Skulisdatter'''  '''married ORM Svendsson "Krypinge-Orm", son of SVEN Svensson & his wife Ragna Ormsdatter (-[1140]).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ASULF Skulesson of Rein & THORA Skoptisdotter, had two children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''GUTTORM Asulfsson of Rein''' .  Snorre names "Guthorm of Reine" as the son of "Asolf of Reine" & his wife[231].  Morkinskinna names “Ásólfr, the father of Guthormr at Rein” as the son of “Skúli, the son of Jarl
2 CONC  Tostig Godwinson”[232]. 
2 CONT >>>>* b)         '''SIGRID'''  married HALLKEL Huk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sigrid Asulfdotter & her husband Halkel Huk had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* i)         ''' JON Halkelsson .  '''married  ([1155]) MARGARETA Haraldsdatter, illegitimate daughter of HARALD "Gille" King of Norway & his mistress.'''   Snorre names "Harald Gille's third daughter…Margaret who was married 
2 CONC to Jon Halkelson, a brother of Simon"[233].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jon & his wife Margareta had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* (a)       '''HALLKEL Jonsson''' (-killed in battle Florevåg near Bergen 3 Apr 1194).  From Blindheim Jarl in Norway.  m (after 19 Jun 1179) as her second husband, '''RAGNHILD Erlingsdatter,''' widow of JON Thorbergsson, daug
2 CONC hter of ERLING Ormsen Skakke & his wife Kristin of Norway .  The Saga of King Sverre records the marriage of "Ragnhild daughter of Earl Erling and Kristin Kings-daughter" and "Halkel son of Jon Hallkelsson"[234]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Hallkel & his wife Raghild had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* (1)       '''RAGNVALD '''Hallkelsson (-murdered Husvik near Drøbak 1217, bur Oslo).  Stormann of the Bagler in Norway. 
2 CONT >>>>* ii)         '''SIMON Skalp''' (-killed in battle 1161).  Snorre names "Simon Skalp, a son of Halkel Huk" when recording his marriage[235].  '''married  (1155) MARIA Haraldsdatter, illegitimate daughter of HARALD "Gille" King
2 CONC  of Norway & his mistress.'''  Snorre names "Harald Gille's second daughter…Maria who was married to Simon Skalp, a son of Halkel Huk"[236].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Simon & his wife Maria had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* (a)       '''NIKOLAS''' Snorre names Nikolas as son of "Simon Skalp, a son of Halkel Huk" & his wife[237].  Snorre records that "Simon Skalp's son, the son of a daughter of King Harald Gille" was proposed as king in 1161[2
2 CONC 38]. 
2 CONT * 2.         '''RAGNHILD Skulisdatter'''  '''married ORM Svendsson "Krypinge-Orm", son of SVEN Svensson & his wife Ragna Ormsdatter (-[1140]).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
