1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Today's historians assume that Snorre's sagas are not historical facts when it comes to the kings living before 11th century, therefore his link to his ancestors has been deleted.=
2 CONT
2 CONT =Tryggve Olavsson=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Also known as Tryggvi Ólafsson and TRYGVE Olavsson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Son of OLAV Geirstadaalf, son of HARALD I "Hårfagre/Harfagri/Fairhair" King of Norway & his third wife Svanhild (-killed in battle Tunsberg 934, bur Tunsberg).'''  The Historia Norwegie names "Olauus" as third son of "Haraldu
2 CONC s Comatus"[192].  Under his father's division of territories, Vingulmark, Raumarike, Vestfold and Thelamark were granted to Olav, Björn, Sigtryg, Frode and Thorgils, Olav inherited the lands of his brother Gutthorm when the latter
2 CONC  was killed in battle[193].  He succeeded on the death of his half-brother Guttorm as King in Glommen to Svinasund and Ranrike.  On the death of his brother Björn, he became king in Vestfold, becoming "upper King" in Viken with th
2 CONC e consent of the people on the abdication of his father in favour of his half-brother Erik[194].  After his father's death he took "all the revenues eastward in Viken" with which Erik was "very ill-pleased"[195].  The latter saile
2 CONC d for Tunsberg in Vike where Olav had joined forces with his half-brother Sigröd and defeated and killed the two of them  
2 CONT *  '''TRYGVE Olavsson''' (-murdered Veggen [968]).  Snorre names Trygve as son of Olav[197].  The Historia Norwegie names "Turgonem" as son of "Olauus filius Haraldi Comari", recording that he was brought up "in prouincia Roumorum
2 CONC "[198].  Along with his cousin Gudrod, he supported his uncle Haakon after the latter's return to Norway and was installed as King in Ranrike and Vingulmark in 935, ruling through an appointee as he was "in the years of childhood"
2 CONC [199].  His uncle King Haakon I appointed Trygve to defend Viken in 946[200].  He was murdered by Gudröd, brother of King Harald[201].  The Historia Norwegie records that "Turgonem" was murdered by the sons of King Erik "Blodøks" 
2 CONC at a place later called "Trugguaroyr id est tumulus Turgonis"[202].  Snorre records his death in 963[203].  m ([960]) as her first husband, ÅSTRID Eiriksdatter, daughter of EIRIK Bjordaskalle, from Oprustader & his wife ---.  The 
