1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Ogmund Ormsson==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Orm Eilivsson, Opplandsjarl and Sigrid Finnsdotter
2 CONT * Birth:	circa 1050 in Oppland, Norway
2 CONT * Death:	Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Project MedLands, Norway Nobility==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''EILIV, son of ---'''
2 CONT
2 CONT m as her second husband, RAGNHILD Haakonsdatter, widow of SKOPTI Skagasson, daughter of HAAKON Sigurdsson "the Mighty" Jarl, Regent of Norway & his wife Thora Skagadotter.  Snorre names Ragnhild as an illegitimate daughter of Haak
2 CONC on whom her father married to "Skopte Skagason, a brother of Thora" (the latter being Haakon's wife)[191].  Morkinskinna names “Ingibjorg, daughter of Hákon jarl” as mother of “one of King Magnus´s chieftains…Ormr”[192].  Snorre n
2 CONC ames Orm as the son of "Ragnhild, a daughter of Earl Hakon the Great"[193]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Eiliv & his wife RAGNHILD had one child==
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''ORM Eilivsson''' (-[1055]).  Snorre names Orm as the son of "Ragnhild, a daughter of Earl Hakon the Great"[194].  A later passage confirms that the mother of "Earl Orm Eilifson" was "Ragnhild, a daughter of Earl Ha
2 CONC kon the Great"[195].  Morkinskinna names “Ingibjorg, daughter of Hákon jarl” as mother of “one of King Magnus´s chieftains…Ormr”[196].  Jarl in Oplandene.  m SIGRID Finsdatter, daughter of FIN Arnesson & his wife Thorberg Halfdans
2 CONC datter.  Snorre records that "Sigrid, Fin [Arnason]'s daughter" was married to "Earl Orm"[197]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Orm & his wife had two children:==
2 CONT * 1)         '''RAGNA Ormsdotter''' Snorre names "Ragna, a daughter of Earl Orm Eilifson and Sigrid, a daughter of Earl Fin Arnason" as mother of "Otto"[203].  m SVEN Svensson, son of ERLING of Gerd & his wife ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2)         '''OGMUND Ormsson'''   Snorre names "Ogmund…a son of Earl Orm Eilifson and Sigrid, a daughter of Earl Fin Arnason"[198].  m ---.  The name of Ogmund´s wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Ogmund & his wife had two children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          MUNAN Ogmundsson (-killed in battle 1137).  Snorre names Munan son of "Ogmund…a son of Earl Orm Eilifson and Sigrid, a daughter of Earl Fin Arnason", when recording his death in battle against the supporters of Inge Ki
2 CONC ng of Norway[199]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         ASTRID Ogmundsdatter .  Snorre names "Astrid, Ogmund's daughter" as the mother of "Karl Sonason"[200].  m SUNE Ivarsson .  A Swedish official.  Sune & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       KARL Sunasson Jarl in Vestgötland.  Snorre names "Astrid, Ogmund's daughter" as the mother of "Karl Sonason"[201].  m as her first husband, BRIGIDA Haraldsdatter, [illegitimate] daughter of HARALD "Gille" King of Norway 
2 CONC & his [wife/mistress]  (-22 Oct, bur Riseberga Abbey.  Snorre records that "King Harald Gille's daughter Brigida" was first married to "the Swedish king Inge Halsteinson, and afterwards to Earl Karl Sonason, and then to the Swedis
2 CONC h king Magnus", noting that she and King Inge Haraldson were cousins by the mother's side, and "at last [she] married Earl Birger Brose"[202].  She married secondly Magnus Henriksson of Denmark, King in Östergötland, and thirdly J
2 CONC arl Birger Brosa [Folkungaätten] (-1202). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' - Project MedLands, Norway Nobility - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm
2 CONT
