1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%9Eorvaldr_%C3%81svaldsson
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorvald Asvaldsson (Old Norse: Þórvaldr Ásvaldsson) was the father of the colonizer of Greenland, Erik the Red, and grandfather of Leif Ericson, who visited North America centuries before Christopher Columbus. Thorvald's father w
2 CONC as Ásvald Ulfsson, whose father was Ulf Oxen-Thorisson, whose father was Oxen-Thorir, brother of Naddodd, discoverer of Iceland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorvald Ásvaldsson was born in Norway. He was exiled from Norway c. 960, during the reign of King Harald Fairhair, for the crime manslaughter. He left with his son Erik to northwest Iceland, where he died before 980.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT translated from https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thorvald_%C3%85svaldsson
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Eirik Raude's saga Thorvald Åsvaldsson's father was Ásvald Úlfsson, son of Ulf, the son of ØKSNES-Tore (Oxna-Thorir), brother of Naddodd, the Norwegian Viking from Agder who according to Landnåmaboka discovered Icelan
2 CONC d in the 800s.
