1 OCCU Landnámsmaður í Reykjavík, Landnamsmand. Først til at bosætte sig i Reykjavík, Landnámsmaður í Reykjavík. „... hann staðfestist fyrstr á Íslandi, svá at menn kunni ættir sínar til at telja“, segir í Sturlungu.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Landnámsmaður í Reykjavík. "... hann staðfestist fyrstr á Íslandi, svá at menn kunni ættir sínar til at telja", segir í Sturlungu.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The first norrøn settler in Iceland. Ingolf took over a huge area around Reykjavik, built the necessary buildings and lived there.  His wife was Hallveig, daughter of Frodi Vemundarson the Elder
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingolf Arnarsson http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingolf_Arnarsson 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingolfr Arnarson https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ing%C3%B3lfr_Arnarson
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingólfur Arnarson https://www.snerpa.is/net/snorri/landnama.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The first permanent settlement in Iceland by Norsemen is believed to have been established at Reykjavík by Ingólfur Arnarson from Norway around AD 870; this is described in Landnámabók, or the Book of Settlement. Ingólfur Arnarson
2 CONC  is said to have decided the location of his settlement using a traditional Norse method; he cast his high seat pillars (Öndvegissúlur) into the ocean when he saw the coastline, then settled where the pillars came to shore. Steam 
2 CONC from hot springs in the region is said to have inspired Reykjavík's name, which loosely translates to Smoke Cove (the city is sometimes referred to as Bay of Smoke or Smoky Bay in English language travel guides)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reykjav%C3%ADk
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LZVG-SQX/ing%C3%B3lfur-arnarson-0844-0910
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Arnarson-1
