1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT The hero of this saga is often confused with his grandson of the same name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ketils saga hoengs is a legendary saga from Iceland on the North Norwegian chieftain Ketil Trout from Ramsta (Hrafnista) in Halogaland. It is one of the sagas called Hrafnistumannasogur surrounding Ketil Trout and his relatives. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ketil grows up to become a rascal and a "Askeladden", but matures and a formidable champion.  He slays a dragon and goes through a number of fights, mostly to defend his daughter. In a fight with Dusti, the king of the Samis, he s
2 CONC lays the king and takes his sword and three nagic aarrowheads of flintstone (Hremsa, Fifa and Flaug). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Together with the giantess, Hrafnhild, Ketil has the son, Grim Shaggy Cheek, who was the father of Orvar-Odd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ketel is traditionally regarded as the father of Hrafnhilda, who married Thorkel of Namdalen and bore him a son, the Icelandic Chieftain,  Ketel Thorkelsson. This grandson also went by the name of Ketil Trout.
