2 CONT 1.         [http://www.geni.com/people/Ragnvald-Eysteinsson/6000000001045491041 RAGNVALD] "the Wise", son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Eystein-Ivarsson-%C2%ABthe-Noisy%C2%BB-Glumra/6000000000701119941?through=6000000001045491041
2 CONC   EYSTEIN] "Glumra/Clatterer" Jarl in Norway & his wife ---] (-[894]).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Eystein the Clatterer, father of the wise counsellor Earl Rognwald the Powerful…”, adding that “Earl Rognwald campaigned with King Hara
2 CONC ld Fine-Hair who gave him charge of North More, South More and Romsdale”[784].  Snorre names "Ragnvald Earl of More, a son of Eystein "Glumra" when recording that he had become a supporter of King Harald who had invested him with 
2 CONC the districts of North More and Raumsdal[785].  Snorre records that he was created Jarl of North and South Möre and of Raumsdal in Norway by Harald I "Hårfagre" King of Norway after his victory at Solskiel [869] against Hunthiof K
2 CONC ing of Möre and Nokve King of Raumsdal[786].  Orkneyinga Saga and Snorre both record that King Harald granted Shetland and Orkney to Ragnvald in compensation for the death of his son Ivar[787].  The Historia Norwegie records that 
2 CONC "principi Rogwaldi" crossed the Solund Sea, destroyed the peoples of the Orkney islands, in the days of "Haraldi Comati regis…Norwegie"[788].  Snorre records that Ragnvald was ambushed in his hall and burned alive by Halfdan Haale
2 CONC g and Gudred Liomi, two of King Harald's sons[789].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         for other children: see Cawley’s NORWEGIAN NOBILITY.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >b)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Hallad-Orkneyjarl/6000000001065274497?through=6000000001045491041   HALLAD] .  Orkneyinga Saga names “[http://www.geni.com/people/Hallad-Orkneyjarl/6000000001065274497?through=60000000010454
2 CONC 91041   Hallad], [http://www.geni.com/people/Hrollaug-Eyjafj%C3%B6r%C3%B0ur/6000000001065449177?through=6000000001045491041   Hrollaug] and the youngest [http://www.geni.com/people/Torf-Einarr-R%C3%B6gnvaldarson/600000000104536986
2 CONC 5  Einar]” as “natural sons” of “Earl Rognwald”[790].  Snorre names "Hallad, the second Einar, the third Hrollaug" as the three sons of "Earl Ragnvald" by concubines, adding that they were all "grown men" when their legitimate bro
2 CONC thers were still children[791].  Jarl [of Orkney].  Orkneyinga Saga records that Ragnvald sent “his son Hallad west to the islands” after hearing of the death of his brother and nephew, and that [http://www.geni.com/people/Harald-
2 CONC I-Halvdansson-%C2%ABFairhair%C2%BB-H%C3%A5rfagre/3950516705030063754  Harald I "Hårfagre" King of Norway] gave “the title of earl” to Hallad who “came to Orkney and took up residence on Mainland”[792].  Snorre records that Earl Ra
2 CONC gnvald installed his son Hallad as Jarl of Orkney after the death of his brother  [http://www.geni.com/people/Sigurd-I-Eysteinsson/6000000001073920184?through=6000000001045491041  Sigurd], but that he resigned the earldom and retu
2 CONC rned to Norway[793].  Orkneyinga Saga records that, following complaints by farmers about Viking raids, Hallad “tiring of his rule, gave up the earldom and went back to Norway as a common landholder” which “made him a laughing sto
2 CONC ck”[794].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >m ---.  The name of Hallad´s wife is not known. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >Hallad & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>i)          [http://www.geni.com/people/%C3%9E%C3%B3rir-Halla%C3%B0arson/6000000001459556020  THORE].  Are´s Landnama-book records that "Thor-rid the daughter of Thore, the son of Earl Hallad, the son of Rogn-wald Earl of More" 
2 CONC married "Thor-gils…"[795].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>(a)        [http://www.geni.com/people/%C3%9Eur%C3%AD%C3%B0ur-%C3%9E%C3%B3risd%C3%B3ttir/6000000001459535013?through=6000000001459556020   THOR-RID] .  Are´s Landnama-book records that "Thor-rid the daughter of Thore, the son o
2 CONC f Earl Hallad, the son of Rogn-wald Earl of More" married "Thor-gils of Thor-gils-stead in Deep-frith, the father of Coll", son of "[http://www.geni.com/people/Thorbjorn-BODMODSSON-B%C3%B6%C3%B0m%C3%B3%C3%B0arson/60000000088296579
2 CONC 39  Thor-beorn Loke]…the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Bodmodur-THORBJORNSSON-%C3%9Eorbjarnarson/6000000008830308730 Bead-mod] of Scut [who] went to Iceland and took in settlement Deep-frith and Gruoch-ness, up to Gowe-frith"
2 CONC , and names their descendants[796].  
2 CONT
