2 CONT They say otherwise about King Sigurd's way of being, that he was difficult to work and took care of much of the frame with gard and goods; he controlled the farm itself. He was not a man of fancy, and he was rather lenient; he was
2 CONC  the wisest man of all that was in Norway at that time, and the richest in movable property, he was peaceful and docile. Asta, his wife, was generous and generous. They had these children: Guttorm, he was the oldest, then Gunnhild
2 CONC , Halvdan, Ingerid and Harald.
