1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Jon Torbergson, på Randeberg=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Jon Torbergsson was a lieutenant and large farmer on Randaberg in Rogaland
2 CONT * Birth:	1153 in Randaberg, Rogaland, Norway
2 CONT * Around 1100, representatives from the Arnunge family at Giske settled on the Randaberg farm on Randabergfjellet
2 CONT * Death:	June 18, 1179 in Kalvskinnet, Åkeren, Trondheim, Sør-Trøndelag, Norway (Falt på slaget ved Kalvskinnet)
2 CONT * Jon Torbergsson is considered a descendant of Erling Skjalgsson's daughter Ragnhild Erlingsdatter and her husband Torberg Arneson at Giske . There is a runic inscription on Indre Bø on Randaberg with the text: "Torberg Torsteins
2 CONC son carried this stone" from the 12th century. It may have been Jon's father.
2 CONT * Jon was a very rich man and owned almost the whole of Randaberg and perhaps most of Hundvåg, he also owned several land properties besides this.
2 CONT * He fell in the battle of Kalvskinnet in Trondheim against the birch bones in 1179. There he made a name for himself before the battle, when he warned against drunkenness.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  [http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Torbergsson '''Ragnhild Erlingsdatter''',] the daughter of Erling Skakke and Kristin Sigurdsdatter and sister of King Magnus Erlingsson and was thus sovger to the king. Jon was a very 
2 CONC wealthy man and owned almost all Randaberg and perhaps most of Hundvåg , he also owned several lands out of it. Jon was also a nobleman and the king's military. He took part including the battle of Kalvskinnet against Birkebeinere
2 CONC n . Where he made his mark before the battle when he warned against drunkenness and drunkenness. Jon fell during the battle in the year 1179 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ragnhild Jonsdatter, 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.aftenbladet.no/meninger/debatt/i/Xg3Glb/grav-ut-den-gamle-kirketuften-fra-vikingtiden-paa-randabergfjellet Great Vessel]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon Torbergsson (1153–1179) was not just anyone. The Lendmen belonged to the country's highest social elite and rank, in the Viking Age and the first part of the Middle Ages only surpassed by earls. Later the title was changed to 
2 CONC baron. The vassals were the king's men who had received land and payment from the king - in return for providing armed men in times of peace and war.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon Torbergsson himself was of high standing with close ties to the royal power in the 12th century. He is considered a descendant of Erling Skjalgsson and was married to Erling Skakke's daughter Ragnhild Erlingsdatter . She was t
2 CONC he sister of King Magnus Erlingsson and became the great-grandmother of Magnus Lagabøte .
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon was a rich landowner with income from his own farm, other properties and royal estates. Most of Randaberg was probably his - the same probably also applied to Hundvåg. In addition, there were probably many other landed propert
2 CONC ies in our part of the country, the historians believe.
2 CONT
2 CONT The king's right to use his vassals in times of war also became Jon Torbergsson's bane, aged 26. Together with Magnus Erlingsson, he fell in 1179 in battle against the Birkebeiners and Sverre Sigurdson in the Battle of Kalvskinnet
2 CONC  in Trondheim. So did nine other members of the public.
2 CONT
2 CONT The king's powerful lieutenant who once lived in Randaberg, has had a central city center street named after him, Jon Torbergssons vei , close to Randaberg church.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Randaberg Gard and Family B1=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Family: Ætt og Heim 1979, s 38: Jon Randaberg og ..., av Sigurd Rygh Garden vart og tidleg stormannssæte. I siste halvdel av 1100-talet veit me det var
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon Torbergsson and his wife Ragnhild Erlingsdotter who prevailed here. Ragnhild (daughter of Erling Skjalgsson) and husband Torberg Arnesson at Giske and belonged to the aristocracy of Arnung. Another descendant of Ragnhild and T
2 CONC orberg at Giske was the daughter's son King Olav Kyrre, father of King Magnus Berrføtt and grandfather of Sigurd Jorsalfare. Daughter of Sigurd Jorsalfare, Kristin, in turn married Erling Skakke. And their daughter was the Ragnhil
2 CONC d who was married to Jon Torbergsson. In this way, I see that Jon, who used to be related to the Norwegian royal family, got the band there further strength. With this gift he was also brother-in-law to King Magnus Erlingsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon was also a loom to King Magnus. It would say that he should support the king militarily and as a local ruler. In return, he earned the proceeds of the extensive land estate Jon himself must have eight. What earthenware he eigh
2 CONC t, do not know me. But it must be reasonable to believe that Randberg and Indre and Ytre BØ belonged to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon accompanied his brother-in-law and father-in-law in the battle with King Sverre with ships and crew. In the evening of June 17, 1179, Erling Skakke and King Magnus lay with their people in Trondheim. After Erling Skakke had di
2 CONC nner, Sigurd Nikolausson and Jon Torbergsson came to him and asked him to put out guards, who had heard the birch bees were on their way to the city. Still, Erling thought they could go to bed, the birch-bellies probably didn't da
2 CONC re to hit now.
2 CONT
2 CONT Then Jon Erling addressed the court in a way that testified to what two were in him: "It should be a good divination to us when the Earl promises us that we will not care for the birch bones; but there were some who said, sir, tha
2 CONC t you put more teams into filling Dives with mead and wine than sewing for the Army Dicks. " Erling was naturally angry, but still put out guards that he was asking for. And Jon went to his ship.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the morning, Sverre fired at the city with 350 men. Erling and Magnus were tempted to gather their men at Kristkyrkja, but large parts of the army lay dead in the city after the day on the road. Three great men nevertheless met
2 CONC  with their people, and the foremost of them is the committee Jon Torbergsson. After prayer in the church, they went with the 600 men they had scraped together to meet Sverre. They meet at the field Kalvskinnet, and there fall bot
2 CONC h Erling Skakke, Jon Torbergsson and a number of other great men. King Magnus escaped by escaping.
2 CONT
2 CONT If Jon falls, however, his descendants will leave deep traces in Norway. Sole Ice was the wife of Duke Skule, Ragnhild Nokkvesdotter, daughter of Jon. And Margrete, daughter of Ragnhild and Skule, was our queen through the marriag
2 CONC e ceremony with King Håkon Håkonsson. Therefore all the Norwegian kings from 1217 to 1387 were descendants of Jon on Randaberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of them was the son of Margrete Skulesdotter, King Magnus Lagabøter. Magnus had been given the royal title in 1258 and the Rygjafylket to rule. The capital of his kingdom was Stavanger where he bid in 1264. Then he moved to Be
2 CONC rgen to be king over the whole kingdom. But he must still have eight lots of land in the Stavanger area, not least as a legacy to his mother. He has part of this land estate added to the third Apostle church in Bergen in 1275, bet
2 CONC ween Anna Indre and Ytre BØ and Randaberg. It is close to threatening that this was inheritance after Jon Torbergsson. Other guards who were added to this foremost of the royal chapel were here at Nord-Jæren Husabø and Austbø at H
2 CONC undvåg, Nedre Tjensvoll and Nordre Sunde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rune inscription from Indre Bø: "Torberg Torsteinsson carried this stone" is from the 1100s. So there is nothing in the way that it is about Jon's father. Perhaps there is a testimony about the connection between the BØ-gardane an
2 CONC d Jon's family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also at Randaberg itself it succeeded in building great men for more than a hundred years after Jon. Around 1280, Eirik Randaberg hosted with a number of high school physicians, lay physicians and clergy in connection with the wil
2 CONC l of Arnbjørn Hebnes. In it he gave silver and earthenware to five churches in Stavanger, five churches in Ryfylke, to Utstein monastery and to Jorsalaland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He himself had rented the garden of the Apostle Church in Bergen, eight other estates, at Randaberg at that time for five years. Therefore, between another Sigurd Randaberg, he could sell half a man's work (about 90 bucks sake) in
2 CONC  Grødem in Randaberg to Orm Tasta one time only in the 1300s.
2 CONT
2 CONT By, Birger Lindanger
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.terra-norwegen.com/Rogaland/FylkerRogalandRandaberg.html Randaberg Municipality: Information / Facts]
2 CONT
2 CONT Randaberg is the third smallest municipality in the Fylke Rogaland and is very densely populated with 327 residents per square meter due to the catchment area of ​​the city of Stavanger . Randaberg is surrounded by water to the no
2 CONC rth, east and west. Viskeviga Bay also cuts deep inland to the south. A little to the east, the border with Stavanger Municipality bisects the approx. 4 km long Hålandsvatn, the municipality's largest lake. The municipality's high
2 CONC est elevation, 
2 CONT at 69 m, is north of the administrative town of Randaberg.
2 CONT Already in the Stone Age - around 12,000 years ago - people settled here. This area is one of the earliest permanent settlements in Norway. At that time, the land was 25 m below today's level, and many parts of today's Randaberg w
2 CONC ere covered with water. These Stone Age people lived in two caves that can still be visited today. 
2 CONT As early as the 11th century, Randaberg was a municipality with the same borders as today. At that time nobleman Jon Torbergson played a large role in society. However, when the plague wiped out most of the country's residents, th
2 CONC e congregation could no longer afford its own priest and it fell under the jurisdiction of Stavanger Municipality. Before becoming an independent municipality again in 1922, it was part of the Hetland administration.
2 CONT Randaberg has remained a typical agricultural community to this day. In 1950 the population was just under 2,000. Today it has grown to over 8,000. The dynamic development of the oil town of Stavanger is also taking hold here. Alt
2 CONC hough agriculture is still a cornerstone of the municipality's economy, industrial and service companies have also settled here in recent decades.
2 CONT Randaberg is in the process of realizing an urban planning project that is unrivaled in Norway: development and execution are the result of a national architectural competition.
2 CONT
2 CONT Randaberg Municipality is located at the northern tip of the peninsula that stretches north-east from Stavanger in the Kvitsøyfjorden and is the northernmost municipality in Jæren County . Only 10 minutes separate them from the ci
2 CONC ty of Stavanger.  Located on the 59th degree of latitude, it is roughly level with the Preikestolen lookout rock on the Lysefjorden and more southerly than the Svinesund Bridge in eastern Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT
