2 CONT På enkelte nettsteder er Pål Torsteinson oppgitt som far til Kolbein på Harildstad, uten videre kildehenvisninger. Den samme Pål Torsteinsen er forøvrig også oppgitt som far til Torstein List. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  Engebret Hougen's Aettesoge for Gudbrandsdalen, including page 110
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift to ganger..
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn av Kolbein Harildstad og ? (?):
2 CONT *Ivar Kolbeinsen Røssum+   f. c 1350, d. e 1394 
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn av Kolbein Harildstad og ? (?):
2 CONT *Arne Kolbeinsen Harildstad+   f. 1358 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1310 in Harildstad, Kvikne, Nord-Fron (OP). Died about 1360 on Harildstad, Kvikne, Nord-Fron (OP).
2 CONT
2 CONT "Kollbæin a Haraldzstaudum" is mentioned only once in the sources. He is among six men who reported to King Magnus that Hr. Sigurd Erlandsen, with witnesses for them, had stated that Sigurd Eldjarn had let read Kong Sverre letter 
2 CONC in the Althing on Rusten after King Magnus's death in 1280, confirmed by the following kings, whereby he gave Ivar old Gæsling on Sundbu Heimdal water, and that Sundbu-men later upåtalt had owned this water. Dated 07.05.1336 Vaage
2 CONC  (DN III 185).
2 CONT
2 CONT It is likely that Kolbein was the father of Ivar Kolbeinsen Rossum. 1  Engebret Hougen: Ættesoge Gudbrandsdalen I, page 101.
2 CONT
2 CONT Det er trolig at Kolbein var far til Ivar Kolbeinsen Røssum. 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Engebret Hougen: Ættesoge for Gudbrandsdalen I, side 101.
