1 OCCU Høvding, High King of Ireland and King of the Cenél nEógain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Niall Caille mac Áedo (c. 791 – 846) was the 166th High King of Ireland and King of Ailech. A dominant ruler from the Cenél nÉogain branch of the Northern Uí Néill dynasty, his reign marked a pivotal turning point 
2 CONC as the Norse-Viking raids transitioned from localized coastal plundering into permanent inland settlements. He earned his famous posthumous epithet Caille from the river in which he met his tragic end.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Áed Oirdnide mac Néill, High King of Ireland (d. 819).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Medb ingen Indregataig, a royal princess of the Uí Briúin of Connacht.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Gormflaith ingen Donnchada, an elite princess of Clann Cholmáin and daughter of High King Donnchad Midi.
2 CONT
2 CONT Niall did not immediately ascend the throne upon his father's death due to the alternating succession rules between the northern and southern Uí Néill branches. He successfully claimed the Kingship of Ailech in 823 and firmly esta
2 CONC blished his supreme northern authority in 827 by winning the historic Battle of Leth Cam, where he decisively crushed the rival kingdoms of Ulster. In 833, he ascended as the High King of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT His long imperial reign was defined by fierce defense of Irish soil. In 844, Niall achieved a monumental military triumph near Armagh, leading his royal forces to completely shatter a massive invading Viking army to save the sacre
2 CONC d monastic city and its people from destruction. Tragically, in 846, while on a military campaign, Niall witnessed one of his personal bodyguards pulled under by the flooded, raging currents of the River Callan. Disregarding his o
2 CONC wn safety, the High King spurred his horse into the torrent to save the man but was swept away and drowned.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Áed Findliath mac Néill (c. 830 – 879) – Celebrated High King of Ireland who aggressively checked Norse expansion.
2 CONT #Duarcán mac Néill
2 CONT #Máel Dúin mac Néill
2 CONT #Flaithbertach mac Néill 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Within the official traditions of Clan MacNeil, Niall is recognized as their 14th Ancestral Chief. While his historical title was High King of Ireland rather than a Scottish clan chief, he represents a crucial link in the traditio
2 CONC nal lineage connecting the clan to the royal Uí Néill dynasty of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
