2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#OlafSihtricsondied981B
2 CONT
2 CONT OLAF [Anlaf] Sihtricson (-Iona [978/80]).  He was accepted as OLAF King of York by the Northumbrians in 927 after the death of his father, and was supported by his uncle Guthfrith who came from Dublin.  However, Æthelstan invaded 
2 CONC Northumbria and expelled Olaf who joined his father's former associates in Ireland[1171].  Florence of Worcester records that "Northhymbrenses" chose "regem Northmannorum Anlafum" as king, undated but dateable to [941] from the co
2 CONC ntext[1172].  Siimeon of Durham records that "the son of Sihtric named Onlaf reigned over the Northumbrians" in 941 but was driven out in 943[1173].  He lost the territories gained by Olaf Guthfrithson to Edmund King of Wessex in 
2 CONC 942, and he was driven out of York and deposed in favour of his cousin Rægnald.  He returned to Northumbria in 944, reasserting himself as king in opposition to Rægnald, but he was expelled by Edmund King of Wessex later that year
2 CONC [1174].  Simeon of Durham records that King Edmund expelled "king…Anlaf the son of Sihtric and [king] Reignold the son of Guthferth" from Northumbria in 944[1175].  Florence of Worcester records that Eadmund King of Wessex expelle
2 CONC d "duos reges, Anlafum regis…Sihtrici filium, et Reignoldum Guthferthi filium" from Northumbria, undated but dateable to [944] from the context[1176].  He returned to York once more in 949, expelling King Erik "Blodøks/Blood-axe",
2 CONC  but was finally driven out in his turn by Erik in 952.  King of Dublin 941/43, 945/49 and 953/981. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        KINGS of DUBLIN.  
2 CONT
2 CONT OLAF [Anlaf] Sihtricsson, son of SIHTRIC King of York & his first wife --- (-Iona [978/80]).  He was accepted as King of York by the Northumbrians in 927 after the death of his father, and was supported by his uncle Guthfrith who 
2 CONC came from Dublin.  However, Æthelstan invaded Northumbria and expelled Olaf, who joined his father's former associates in Ireland[1036].  He joined his cousin at York in 940 and was elected King of York[1037].  Simeon of Durham re
2 CONC cords that "the son of Sihtric named Onlaf reigned over the Northumbrians" in 941 but was driven out in 943[1038].  He lost the territories gained by Olaf Guthfrithson to Edmund King of Wessex in 942, and he was driven out of York
2 CONC  and deposed in favour of his cousin Rægnald.  He returned to Northumbria in 944, reasserting himself as king in opposition to Rægnald, but he was expelled by Edmund King of Wessex later that year[1039].  Simeon of Durham records 
2 CONC that King Edmund expelled "king…Anlaf the son of Sihtric and [king] Reignold the son of Guthferth" from Northumbria in 944[1040].  He returned to York once more in 949, expelling King Erik "Blodøks/Blood-axe", but was finally driv
2 CONC en out in his turn by Erik in 952.  King of Dublin 941/43, 945/49 and 953/981.  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Olaf son of Sitric high-king over the Foreigners of Dublin” died in Iona in [978/79] after being defeated by “Mae
2 CONC l-Sechnaill the Great”[1041], the battle being dated between 978 and 980 in different sources (see below). 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly (after 952) as her second husband, ---, widow of DOMNALL, daughter of ---.  Her marriages are confirmed by the Annals of Tigernach which record that “MaelSechnaill son of Domnall and Glún iarainn (Ironknee) son of Olaf, 
2 CONC son of MaelSechnail´s mother” defeated “Domnall Clóen, son of Lorcán, and Imar of Waterford” in [981/82][1042]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly as her first husband, GORMLAITH, daughter of MURCHAD MacFinn King of Leinster & his wife --- (-1030).  She married secondly Brian Boru, and thirdly, as his [third] wife, Maelsechnaill King of Ireland.  The Annals of Tig
2 CONC ernach record the death in 1030 of “Gormlaith, daughter of Murchad son of Fland” mother of “Sitric son of Olaf king of the Foreigners and of Donnchad son of Brian king of Munster”[1043].  The Annals of the Four Masters record the 
2 CONC death in 1030 of “Gormlaith daughter of Murchadh son of Finn, mother of the king of the foreigners Sitric, Donnchadh son of Brian king of Munster, and Conchobhar son of Maeleachlainn king of Teamhair”[1044]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf & his [first] wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.             RAGNALL (-killed in battle Temair [978/80]).  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 980 of "Ragnall son of Amlaíb" at the battle of Temair[1045].  The Annals of the Four Masters record that “Ragnhall son of Amhla
2 CONC eibh heir to the sovereignty of the foreigners” was killed in 978 in “the battle of Teamhair”[1046].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Ragnall, son of Olaf, crownprince of the Foreigners” was killed in battle by “Mael Sechnail
2 CONC l the Great, son of Domnall, son of Donnchad, son of Fland” at “Tara” in [978/79][1047].  
2 CONT
2 CONT [m ---.  The name of Ragnall´s wife is not known.  Ragnall & his wife had [one possible child]: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.             --- “Glun iaraind/Iron knee” (-murdered [987/89]).  The Annals of Tigernach record that “MaelSechnaill son of Domnall and Glún iarainn (Ironknee) son of Olaf, son of MaelSechnail´s mother” defeated “Domnall Clóen, s
2 CONC on of Lorcán, and Imar of Waterford” in [981/82][1048].  King of Dublin.  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 989 of "Glún Iarn king of the foreigners…killed when drunk by his own slave"[1049].  The Annals of Tigernach record
2 CONC  that “Glún iarainn (Ironknee) son of Olaf king of the Foreigners” was killed “by his own slave…Colbain” in [987/88][1050].  m ---.  The name of his wife is not known.  One child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)             GILLA Ciaráin (-killed in battle Clontarf 23 Apr 1014).  The Annals of Ulster record that "Brian son of Ceinnéitig son of Lorcán king of Ireland and Mael Sechnaill son of Domnall king of Temair" led an army to “Áth 
2 CONC Cliath” in 1014, adding that “Gilla Ciarráin son of Glún Iairn, heir designate of the foreigners” was killed in the battle[1051]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf & his [second] wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.             SIHTRIC (-1042).  King of Dublin.  The Annals of Ulster record that "Sitriuc son of Amlaíb was expelled from Áth Cliath" in 994[1052].  The Annals of the Four Masters record that “Imhar came to Ath-Cliath after Sitr
2 CONC ic, son of Amblaeibh” in 994[1053].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Ragnall was killed by the Leinstermen, Imar again fled, and Sitric reigned in his place” in [993/94][1054].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Sitriuc so
2 CONC n of Olaf king of the Foreigners” plundered “into Ulster…Cell Cleithe and Inis Cumscraig” in [1000/01][1055].  Orkneyinga Saga records that Sigurd Jarl of Orkney went to Ireland “five years after the Battle of Svoldur” to support 
2 CONC “King Sigtrygg Silk-Beard” against “King Brian of Ireland”, and left “his elder sons in charge of the earldom”, but was killed in the battle in which King Brian was killed[1056].  The Annals of Ulster record that "Sitriuc grandson
2 CONC  of Amlaíb king of the foreigners" went to Rome in 1028[1057].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Sihtric´s wife is not known.  Sihtric & his wife had six children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)             ARTALACH (-killed in battle Glenn Mama 30 Dec [996/97]).  The Annals of Tigernach name “Artalach son of Sitric and Harald son of Olaf, and Cuilen son of Erigen” among those killed in battle in [996/97] by “Mael Sech
2 CONC lainn and Brian son of Kennedy” at “Glenn Mama”[1058]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)             OLAF (-killed in battle 1013).  The Annals of Ulster record that "Amlaíb son of Sitriuc…the son of the king of the foreigners and Mathgamain son of Duibgilla son of Amlaíb" were killed in 1013 by “Cathal son of Donn
2 CONC chad son of Dub dá Bairenn”[1059]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)             --- “Glun iaraind/Iron knee” (-killed 1031).  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Iron-knee son of Sitric” was killed by “the (folk of) the south of Bregia” in 1031[1060].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of his wife is not known.  One child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)               son .  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Gofraidh son of Sitric” was killed in Wales “by the son of Iron-Knee” in 1036[1061]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)             OLAF ([after 1013]-murdered 1034).  The Annals of Ulster record that "Amlaíb son of Sitriuc king of the foreigners was held prisoner by Mathgamain ua Riacáin king of Brega" in 1029 and ransomed for "1,200 cows and s
2 CONC ix score Welsh horses and sixty ounces of gold…"[1062].  He was presumably born after the death of his brother Olaf in 1013, unless one or other of these sons was illegitimate.  The Annals of Ulster record that "Amlaíb son of Sitr
2 CONC iuc was killed by the Saxons on his way to Rome"[1063].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Olaf son of Sitric was killed by Englishmen as he was going to Rome” in 1034[1064].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Olav´s wife is not known.  Olav & his wife had one child:   
2 CONT
2 CONT i)               SIHTRIC (-killed in battle Isle of Man 1073).  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1073 of "Sitriuc son of Amlaib and two grandsons of Brian…killed in Man”[1065]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT e)             GODFRID (-killed Wales 1036).  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Gofraidh son of Sitric” was killed in Wales “by the son of Iron-Knee” in 1036[1066]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT f)               RAGNHILD .  m CYNAN ap Iago, son of IAGO ap Idwal King of Gwynedd & his wife --- (-1060).  He was exiled to Ireland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf & his [---] wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.             HARALD (-killed in battle Glenn Mama 30 Dec [996/97]).  The Annals of Ulster record that "Aralt son of Amlaíb" was killed in battle at Glenn Mama "III Kal Jan" 999[1067].  The Annals of Tigernach name “Artalach son 
2 CONC of Sitric and Harald son of Olaf, and Cuilen son of Erigen” among those killed in battle in [996/97] by “Mael Sechlainn and Brian son of Kennedy” at “Glenn Mama”[1068].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Harald´s wife is not known.  Harald & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)             IMAR (-1054).  King of Dublin.  The Annals of the Four Masters record that “the son of Aralt was expelled by the foreigners” in 1046 and “the son of Raghnall was elected king”[1069].  The Annals of Tigernach record 
2 CONC that “Imar son of Harald” slaughtered “Ragnall Húa Eochada” in “Rathlin of the Ulaid”[1070].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1054 of "Ímar son of Aralt, king of the foreigners"[1071].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Imar´s wife is not known.  Imar & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)               GODFRID (-1095).  King of Dublin.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Goffraidh, son of Harald´s son” became king of Dublin in 1091[1072].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1095 of "Gofrai
2 CONC dh Meranach, king of the foreigners"[1073].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record the death in 1095 of “Gobfraidh rex Dormanorom”[1074]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.             DUBGAL (-killed in battle Clontarf 1014).  The Annals of Ulster record that "Dubgall son of Amlaíb" was killed in battle at Clontarf in 1014[1075]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.             GYDA .  Snorre records the betrothal and marriage of Olaf Trygvason to "a queen called Gyda…a sister of Olaf Kvaran who was king of Dublin in Ireland [who] had been married to a great earl in England" after whose de
2 CONC ath "she was at the head of his dominions"[1076].  In a later passage, Snorre refers to "King Olaf Kvaran" as his wife's father[1077].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ---.  m secondly (in England 988) as his second wife, OLAV Trygveson, son of TRYGVE Olavsson [Norway] & his wife Åstrid Eiriksdatter (posthumously [968][1078]-drowned Øresund o. b. Svold, near Rügen 9 Sep [1000]).  He im
2 CONC posed himself as OLAV I King of Norway in [995]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.             MAELMAIRE (-1021).  The Annals of the Four Masters record the death in 1021 of “Maelmaire daughter of Amhlaeibh, wife of Maelseachlainn son of Domhnall”[1079].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m as his third wife, MAELSECHNAILL King of Ireland, son of DOMNALL & his wife --- ([949/50]-Cró Inis of Lough Ennell 2 Sep 1022).  
