2 CONC son of Sitric Caoch ua Ímair, rí Dubgall & Finngall and unknown (?).4,5,6,7 Amlaíb Cuarán mac Sitric of Dublin was taken from York to Dublin, Ireland by his Uncle?, Guthfrith, in 927. He and Gothfraidh ua Ímair were expelled from 
2 CONC York by King Aethelstan of Wessex in 927. Amlaíb Cuarán mac Sitric of Dublin went to Cair-Abroc in 938.11 Annals of the Four Masters 938: "A victory was gained by the King of the Saxons over Constantine, son of Aedh; Anlaf, or Amh
2 CONC laeibh, son of Sitric; and the Britons. / Cath-raoinedh ria righ Saxan for Constantin mac Aedha for Anlaf no Amhlaoibh, mac Sitric, & for Breathnaibh." ( (an unknown value)).12 He was baptized in 941; "A.D. 941. This year King Edm
2 CONC und received King Anlaf at baptism."13 He was chosen as their king by the Northumbrians who abandoned their allegiance to the Angles of Wessex an Athelstan's death in 941.13 He succeeded his 1st cousin, Olaf I, to the throne of Du
2 CONC blin in 941. King of York at England between 941 and 943.5,14 He was a witness where Edmund I "the Magnificent", King of the English moved against Olaf Sihtricson and regained the lands lost to the former Olaf in 942.15 Amlaíb Cua
2 CONC rán mac Sitric of Dublin was a witness where Edmund I "the Magnificent", King of the English made peace with Olaf and saw him baptised as a Christian in 943.16 Amlaíb Cuarán mac Sitric of Dublin remained in Dublin after Blacaire, 
2 CONC one of the chiefs of the foreigners, was expelled in 943 at Dublin, Ireland.17 He was a witness where Edmund I "the Magnificent", King of the English took advantage of the fighting that broke out between Olaf Sihtricson and a riva
2 CONC l claimant to the Scandanavian Kingdom of York, and invaded Northumbria and brought it under his rule in 944.16 Amlaíb Cuarán mac Sitric of Dublin was restored to the throne of York following Ragnald II, but soon lost it to the En
2 CONC glish King Eadred in 944. King of York, restored at England in 944. He was succeeded his 1st cousin, Blacar, to the throne of Dublin in 945.14,10 King of Dublin at Ireland between 945 and 948.14 He was restored to the throne of Yo
2 CONC rk, succeeding Eric Bloodaxe, with the help of Eadred in 949. King of York, restored at England between 949 and 952.14 He was restored to the throne of Dublin in 953.14 King of Dublin, restored between 953 and 980.14 He married Go
2 CONC rmlaith ingen Murchada Uí Fáeláin, daughter of Murchad mac Finn Uí Fáeláin, rí Laigin and N. N. ingen Taidg Uí Conchobair, before 980; One of her 6.1,18 Amlaíb Cuarán mac Sitric of Dublin abdicated his throne after the Battle of T
2 CONC ara in 980.5,19,10 Annals of Tigernach 980: "Amlaim mac Sitriuca, aird-righ ar Gallaib Atha Cliath, do dul co h-Í a n-aithrighe & a n-ailithri iarsin cath mortuus est."20 He was called the High King of the "foreigners" in Ath Clia
2 CONC th, or Dublin, in the Annals of Tigernach.20 He died in 981 at Ionia. He died in religious retirement.1,3,21,10,22,9
