1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Lendmann Guttorm Åsolvsson, paa Rein=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Guttorm, was the  son of  Åsulv Skulesson på Rein og Tora * Skoftesdotter.
2 CONT * Guttorm lived at Rein and seems to have lived very long. He was probably the head of Skule Tostesson's highly regarded family in 1183.
2 CONT * Guthorm Aasolvsen, paa Rein. Guthorm was a son of Aasolv Skuleson. In 1136 he attended the assembly in Trondheim, together with other ndheim, together with other leaders and chieftains when Sigurd III Mouth was proclaimed King o
2 CONC f Norway
2 CONT * Born possibly in Rein i Rissa, Fosen, Sør-Trøndelag, Norge 
2 CONT * He is referred to as one of the countrymen who, after Harald Gilles died in 1136, supported Harald's son, Sigurd Munn. He was Sigurd's guardian and got him elevated to the throne. Guttorm and his entire family were closely assoc
2 CONC iated with the Trønder Party around Sigurd Mund and Haakon 
2 CONT * Guttorm Asulfsson lived at Rein, Austria.
2 CONT * Lendmann. Lived from 1120 to 1183.
2 CONT * Guttorm lived on reindeer and seems to have lived very long. He was well in 1183, head of Skule Tostensson's highly-regarded ancestry. He is referred to as one of the loins men who, after Harald Gilles' death in 1136, supported 
2 CONC Harald's son, Sigurd the mouth. He was Sigurd's guardian and had him elevated to the throne. Guttorm and his entire ancestry were close to the Trøndelag party around Sigurd Mund and Haakon Herdebreid.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Inges Saga: 1.... When the tithes came north to Trondheim that King Harald (Gille) was by Dage, Sigurd, son of King Harald, was taken to King there, And with this decision was Ottar birting, Peter Saue-Ulvs
2 CONC son and Brødrene Guttorm Åsolvsson from Rein and Ottar Balle and many other chieftains.
2 CONT
