1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Borghild Gudbrandsdotter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Husfrue på Gjerde gnr 9/1 Etne i Hordaland'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Borghild var født på Hundorp gnr 68/1 Sør-Fron Oppland datter av Dala Gudbrand og Ossa
2 CONT * Hun var gift med Erlend Ølvesson fra Gjerde, de hadde sønnen Svein
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde :
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.: Mervyn Archdall: The Peerage of Ireland, Vol VII [1789] - a revised and enlarged version of John Lodges editon [1754] (https://play.google.com/store/books/details?id=eYsUAAAAYAAJ&rdid=book-eYsUAAAAYAAJ&rdot=1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gouldbrand (Dale-Gudbrand?), the third and great Hersa of Gouldbrandsdall, was the first we mentioned as a Christian, to which faith he was converted by St. Olaus, the pious, King of Norway. — He kept his court at Brown (Fron?), w
2 CONC here he built a church, and having married Ossa, daughter of Suend, the sirst Earl of Orkney and Shetland, had issue by her three sons and two daughters, viz.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gouldbrand ;
2 CONT * Forbrand, of whom hereafter;
2 CONT * Colbrand [who attended St. Olaus into England, where he was slain by Hugh Earl of Warwick. — He married Raugnhilda, daughter of Sigurd of Leirollen in Walders (Valdres?), and from him are descended the Knights of Gouldbransdall,
2 CONC  and many families of repute in Norway and England]; daughter 
2 CONT * Wilfhilda, who married Finkol, a distinguished Nobleman of Sliva in Walders (Valdres); and
2 CONT * '''Broghilda (Borghilda?), who married Erling (Erlend?) of Gierda (Gjerde?), a Noble Lord of Sagn (Sogn?), by whom she was ancestor of Magnus Erlingson, King of Norway.'''
