2 CONT * Saxo Grammaticus, Danmarks krønike. København; Asschenfeldt’s Stjernebøger, 1985, II, pp. 81.
2 CONT * Det norske folks historie / VI / 466 - http://runeberg.org/detnorsk/6/0476.html
2 CONT * Gerhard Schønings Norges riiges historie ...: deel. Fortale [af P. F. Suhm, by Gerhard Schøning - https://books.google.com/books?id=Oz9JAQAAMAAJ&pg=PT1&lpg=PT1&dq=Finn+Skjalge&source=bl&ots=Z8WWZeKbwS&sig=ACfU3U2AySVNIi2Yg3hmmQ1
2 CONC mJNKpmeBwbA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjH_oSDzIzqAhURXM0KHSFzCe84ChDoATAEegQIAhAB#v=onepage&q=Finn%20Skjalge&f=false
2 CONT * Ulwencreutz's The Royal Families in Europe V, by Lars Ulwencreutz - https://books.google.com/books?id=fpQlBgAAQBAJ&pg=PA373&lpg=PA373&dq=Ulvhild+H%C3%A5kansdotter&source=bl&ots=cwktN8USd7&sig=ACfU3U37EZn_2-pauEKYp4spF463aWtOfg&h
2 CONC l=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjR5suI_ozqAhUPVc0KHUPTCqc4FBDoATAGegQIBxAB#v=onepage&q=Ulvhild%20H%C3%A5kansdotter&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulvhild Håkansdotter (Swedish: Ulfhild, English: Wulfhild, Wolfhild), (c. 1095–c. 1148), was a Scandinavian queen, twice queen consort of Sweden (c. 1117–25 and c. 1134–48) and once queen consort of Denmark (c. 1130–34), married t
2 CONC o King Inge II of Sweden, King Niels of Denmark and King Sverker I of Sweden. Ulvhild had an important role in the Nordic dynastic connections of her time, but the sources are unfortunately insufficient to map the closer circumsta
2 CONC nces. She is mentioned as a femme fatale of high-medieval Scandinavia, as well as a benefactor of the Catholic Church. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulvhild_H%C3%A5kansdotter
