2 CONT
2 CONT [ARNKEL (-killed Stainmore, Westmoreland 954).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Arnkel…Erlend and…Thorfinn Skull-Splitter” as the three sons of Einar[191].  Snorre names "Earls Arnkel and Erlend, the sons of Earl Torfeinar" when recording 
2 CONC that they accompanied King Eirik "Blodøks" from Orkney to plunder the Hebrides and Ireland, but were defeated and killed with King Eirik[192].  Joint Jarl of Orkney with his brothers.  Snorre records that "Arnkel, Erlend and Thorf
2 CONC in Hausakljufer" succeeded their father but that the first two were killed "in a war expedition"[193].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Orkneyinga Saga records that “Earls Arnkel and Erlend, the sons of Turf-Einar” joined ex-King Eirik after he was expelled from Northumbria by Edmund King of England and that they sailed to the Hebrides, looted in Ireland and Strat
2 CONC hclyde, until they were killed in battle against Olaf King of Northumbria[194].]  
2 CONT
