1 NOTE Eirik (Eric) Blood-Ax: described as "tall, well-built, courageous, and
2 CONT good
2 CONT looking.  He was also surly, taciturn, covetous and reckless, but a great
2 CONT and very successful warrior. (Fagrskinna).
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Bloodaxe, the Norseman, was ejected from York hwere he had ruled over the Viking Kingdom, after being expelled from Norway.  The Scandinavian settlements on the island were then under the control of the English.
