1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Hunda-Steinar, Jarl in England==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:	circa 783, in Norway
2 CONT * Death:	circa 839 in Uppsala, Uppsala County, Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Hunda Steinar was married to '''Olof Ragnarsdóttir,''' (786 n.), A daughter of the legendary Ragnar Lodbrok and several children were born that relationship: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Björn Hunda-Steinar Eiríksson''' (also Hundasteinarsson, [ 5 ] 810-880), father of Auðunn skökull Bjarnarson .
2 CONT *''' Eiríkur Hunda-Steinar Eiríksson jarl''' (n. 814), father of Sigurður Bjodaskalle Eriksson, in turn father of Viking-Kåre .
2 CONT * '''Isgerd Eiríksdóttir,''' who married the jarir Thorir of Värmland .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Hunda-Steinar, Wikipedia - https://es.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunda-Steinar
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source texts:
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Landnámabók
2 CONT https://www.snerpa.is/net/snorri/landnama.htm
2 CONT === Chapter
2 CONT
2 CONT Hunda-Steinar was named Earl of England; he had Alfa, daughter of Ragnar fur coat. Their children were Björn, the father of Audun Skökull, and Eiríkur, the father of Sigurd's bidding, and Isgerður, who had Earl Thorir in Vermaland
2 CONC i.
2 CONT
2 CONT Audun Skokull went to Iceland and settled at Víðidal and lived at Audunstadir. With (him) came Thorgils his prodigious companion, the father of Thorarin the god. Audun Skokull was the father of Thora Moshal, mother of Ulfhild, mot
2 CONC her of Asta, mother of King Olaf the Holy. The son of Audun Skokull was Asgeir to Asgeirsá; he had Jorunn, the daughter of the old Ingimund. Their children were Thorvaldur, father of Dalla, mother of Gissur the bishop, and Audun, 
2 CONC father of Asgeir, father of Audun, father of Egil, who had Ulfheeda, daughter of Eyjolfur Gudmundsson's son, and their son Eyjolfur, who was slain in the Althing, father of Orm, chaplain. Bishop. Another son of Audun Skokull was E
2 CONC ystein, father of Thorstein, father of Helgi, father of Thororm, father of Odd, father of Hallbjorn, father of Sighvat the priest. Asgeir's daughter at Asgeirsá was Thorbjörg classmate.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==The Book of Settlements: Landnámabók
2 CONT [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=jj6cIwMCZqIC&redir_esc=y Translated by Hermann Palsson]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===177. Audun skökull 
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a jarl in England called Hunda-Steinar. He married Álöf, Ragnar loðbrók’s daughter, and their children were Bjorn, father of Audun skökull, Eirik, father of Sigurd Bjodaskallo and Isgerd who married Earl Thorir of Vermal
2 CONC and.
2 CONT
2 CONT Audun skökull went to Iceland, tookk possession of Vididale and lived at Audunsstead. His comrade Thorgils Gjallandi, father of Thorarin the Priest, came to Iceland with him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Audun skökull was father of Thora Mosháls , mother of Ulfhild, mother of Asta, mother of King Olaf the Holy. Audun had a son called Asgier of Asgiers River, who married Jorunn, daughter of Ingimund the Old. Their children were Tho
2 CONC rvald, father of Dalla, mother of Bishop Gizur, and the Audun, father of Asgeir, father of Audun, father of Egil who married Ulfheid, daughter of Eyjolf Gudmundarson, and their son was Eyjolf, who was killed at the Althing, the fa
2 CONC ther of Bishop Thorlak’s chaplain, Orm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Audun skökull had another son called Eystein, father of Thorstein, father of Helgi, father of Thororm, father of Odd, father of Halbjørn, father of Sigvat the Priest. Asgeir of Asgeirs River had a daughter Thorbjørg Bekkjarbót.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
