1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anonymous mother of Ragnvald's sons: Torf-Einar, Hallad and Hrollaug. Ragnvald possibly had more than one mistress (=frille). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Orkney saga, the brothers Einar, Hallad (Haddad) and Ivar are referred to as "frillesønner", sons of a frille (=literally mistress, or partner - "concubine" is not a good term for Nordic countries). Whether Ragnvald's four 
2 CONC illegitimate sons Einar, Hrollaug, Hallad and Ivar had the same mother is not known, but highly unlikely.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Harald Hårfagres (Fairhair) saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Earl Ragnvald was King Harald's dearest friend, and the king had the greatest regard for him. He was married to Hild, a daughter of Rolf Nefia, and their sons were Rolf and Thorer. Earl Ragnvald had also three sons by concubines,
2 CONC  -- the one called Hallad, the second Einar, the third Hrollaug; and all three were grown men when their brothers born in marriage were still children Rolf became a great viking, and was of so stout a growth that no horse could ca
2 CONC rry him, and wheresoever he went he must go on foot; and therefore he was called Rolf Ganger."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Groa (Ermina) of Trondheim
2 CONT
2 CONT B: abt 0834 Maer, Nord Trondelag, Norway
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Groa is not mentioned in the sagas - sources? 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ragnvald had three sons by a frille (mistress), her name is not known. Then he married Hild Rolfsdotter, and they had Rolf (Rollo) and Tore (Teiande), also possibly Ivar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other wives or partners are not known, also no daughters are known. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ermina, a concubine, married Rögnvaldr Eysteinsson, Mørejarl, son of Eysteinn Glumra, Jarl of the Uplanders and Aseda Rögnvaldsdóttir, before 870--she was a "more Danico" or "Danish wife."
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p101.htm#i12258 )
2 CONT
