2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Earl Folke Birgersson (Folkunga) and Ulfhild Sunesdotter 
2 CONT * Holmger Folkesson (Ama) , Swedish knight , mentioned as living no later than 1254. Son of Earl Folke . Ancestor of the Ama family , whose coat of arms was a shield cut of stone gables in blue and gold. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Kristina Fastesdotter''' to Landsjö , Kimstad in Östergötland.  HOLMGER Folkason (-after 1264). married CHRISTINA Fastadotter, from Landasjö. - https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDISH%20NOBILITY.htm#HOLMGER Folkason
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''SUNE Folkason''' (-1247).  Jarl in Sweden.  m HELENA Sverkersdatter of Sweden, daughter of SVERKER II Karlsson "den yngre" King of Sweden & his first wife Bengte Ebbesdatter [Galen].  A charter dated 1237 refers to the marria
2 CONC ge of “S. Fulconis ducis filius” and “E. Suerchonis Regis filia” after her abduction from Vreta convent
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ulf Holmgersson (Ama)''' Knight before 1276, Riksråd 1288 , died after 1290. Married: (1) Ulf Holmgersson is mentioned no earlier than 1276 and is then called a knight. He is mentioned as a councilor in 1288 and still alive i
2 CONC n 1290. He was first married to Cecilia Haraldsdotter, daughter of Harald Gudmundsson ( winged lily ). They had four sons. Married: (2) In 1284, Ulf Holmgersson received a papal permit to marry his bride Helena Siggesdotter, with 
2 CONC her he had three daughters and a son. (See: SDHK No: 1266)
2 CONT * '''BENGTA] Folkadotter'''  married JOHAN Ängel
2 CONT * '''NN Folkadotter''' married RÖRIK 
2 CONT * '''NN Folkadotter''' married ULF Karlsson "Fase" [Folkunge] Jarl in Sweden (-[1247/48]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=holmger&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_284&tab=post#tab 284]
2 CONT
2 CONT King Knut (Eriksson) confirms with a witness gift certificate that he donated the part of the fishing in Älvkarleby that is called "bol" to Mariakyrkan in Julita and the convention there and orders that none of his successors may 
2 CONC take back this donation or annul it. Witnesses on behalf of the king are Earl Birger, his brother Karl, the queen's brother Knut, the king's grandson / grandson el. nephew Holmger and Finvid, and witnesses on behalf of the church 
2 CONC are Archbishop Peter in Uppsala, Bishop Vilhelm in Strängnäs, Bishop Kol in Linköping, Bishop Jarpulf in Skara, Bishop Stenar in Växjö, and all the abbots, domprost and nobles in the kingdom. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/
2 CONC sdhk/284.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=holmger&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=4&postid=sdhk_628&tab=post#tab 628]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1250 without day'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Holmger ("H"), Folke jarls son , to his niece Queen K (atarina) and to his sister K (atarina), prioress in Gudhem's monastery, with the promise that he will defend the gifts the queen has given to the said monastery. - https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/photo/view/6000000001669618325?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000143083974821
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=holmger&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=5&postid=sdhk_642&tab=post#tab 642]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1250 June 11, of Issue: Gudhem
2 CONT
2 CONT Queen Catherine of Swedenestablishes on the advice of Earl B (irger), Bishop L (ars) of Skara, his uncle H (olmger) and others. her will and donates to the monastery in Gudhem "Thwlshamar" and "Withem" with additions, "Lindhø", "S
2 CONC lacu" with the land in Kind, Nyköping and whatever she owns there, and everything she owns of movable and immovable property in Västergötland and her part in Denmark on condition that the return of these possessions goes to the co
2 CONC nstruction of the monastery; to Mr. Rörik's children she leaves Strand (in Jäders sn, Österrekarne hd) and to Mr. Johannes Angelus' children “Lvndbv” and the land, which returns 1/2 land money a year; to her uncle Holmger she leav
2 CONC es Tift (in Kärna sn, Hanekinds hd) with additions and to her sister B. Söderköping with additions and all the property and estates that her father Sune had bought; furthermore, she sets aside farms in "Grænnum", "Rugbiarger", "Lj
2 CONC unbv", "Siringj", "Høtofter", "Kilum" and "Kilhambrar" to be distributed among the monastic orders; other movable property and whatever accrues to her from the king's side, she sets aside for pious purposes and to be distributed a
2 CONC s alms in accordance with the discretion of the earl, the scarab, and her uncle Holmger.
2 CONT King Valdemar, Earl Birger, the bishop of Skara, Mr. Holmger and others. seals.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Valdemar, Earl Birger, the bishop of Skara, '' 'Mr. Holmger' '' and others. seals. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001669618325?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000143086735821
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=holmger&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=6&postid=sdhk_653&tab=post#tab 653]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1251 January 17, of Issue: Wallum'''
2 CONT
2 CONT King Valdemar announces that Queen Katarina with the consent of her sister Bengta and her uncle Holmger to the monastery in Gudhem donated "withem" with additions, "Lyndhø", "Slaka" with the land in Kind, Nyköping and whatever she
2 CONC  owns there, and everything she owns of movable and immovable property in Västergötland with compensation for this to her sister in Östergötland, as well as all her properties in Denmark on condition that the return of these goes 
2 CONC to the construction of the monastery. Seals have been attached by the king, his father, Mr. Holmger, Mrs. Bengta, Archbishop J. in Uppsala and his suffragettes, Östergötland's lawyer Magnus, Västergötland's lawyer Peter and all ot
2 CONC her lawyers and wise gentlemen in the kingdom. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/653.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-Bengtsson-Folkunga/6000000002572920173 Magnus], Västergötlands lagman [https://www.geni.com/people/Peter/6000000003414786001 Peter] and all the other lawyers and wise men in the kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=%22holmger+folkesson%22&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_702&tab=post#tab 702]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1254 without day, of Issue: Ramshammar'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Kristina Fastesdotter ("C"), widow of Holmger (Folkesson), announces that she made a land exchange with the prioress M. in Fogdö (Vårfruberga) in such a way that she herself received 8 herbs in Norrlänna and in exchange gave 
2 CONC the prioress 8 herbs and 6 money countries in Söderlänna. The witnesses are her son Lars, Ragnvald "neighbor", Ulf, Kettilbjörn, Elof and "Ofegus" and others. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001669618325?album_type=photos
2 CONC _of_me&end=&photo_id=6000000143091113833&project_id=&start=&tagged_profiles=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=700&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_700&tab=post#tab 700]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1254 without day'''
2 CONT
2 CONT B. and K., Lucia's sons , announce that they gave their three sisters everything they owned in Gösslunda and Brunnåsa, but that the abbess of Gudhem had every right to own or sell the third of the gift that went to their sister In
2 CONC gegerd for the benefit of the monastery. The witnesses were King "W" (Aldemar), "B" (irger) earl and his wife 'the Duchess' "J" (ngeborg) and "H" (olmger) Folkesson and others.
2 CONT
2 CONT Content: [https://www.geni.com/people/Bengt-Karlsson-Folkunga%C3%A4tten/6000000006127494035 B]. And [https://www.geni.com/people/Karl-Karlsson-Ulv/6000000003349367528 K]., [https://www.geni.com/people/Lucia/6000000004848913637 Luc
2 CONC ias] sons, announce that they have given their three sisters all that they possessed i [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%B6sslunda Gösslunda] and Brunnåsa, but that [https://www.geni.com/people/Katarina-Folkesdotter-Folkunga%C3%
2 CONC A4tten/6000000008763369750 had the full right to, for the benefit of the convent, possess or sell the third of the gift which went to their sister [https://www.geni.com/people/Ingegerd-Karlsdotter-Folkunga%C3%A4tt/6000000006127494
2 CONC 073 Ingegerd]. Witnesses were king [https://www.geni.com/people/Valdemar-I-kung-av-Sverige/6000000003455608992 ”W”(aldemar)],[https://www.geni.com/people/Birger-jarl/6000000010160609967 ”B”(irger) jarl] and his wife [https://www.g
2 CONC eni.com/people/Ingeborg-Eriksdatter-Prinsesse-af-Sverige/6000000025029989899 ’ Duchess”J”(ngeborg)] and ''' ”H”(olmger) Folkesson''' m.fl. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/700.pdf
2 CONT
