1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT The Yngling saga - Yngling dynasty Freya1. One, wife - Frigg.
2 CONT
2 CONT “The large mountain range stretches from northeast to southwest (Ural Mountains). It separates Greater Sweden from other countries. The Country of Turks is located not far south of it. Odin had great possessions there. In those da
2 CONC ys, the rulers of the Romans went on campaigns around the world and conquered all nations, and many rulers then fled from their possessions. "
2 CONT
2 CONT “ He put his brothers Ve and Vili as rulers in Asgard, and he set out on a journey and with him all the Dii and many other people. He went first west to Gardariki and then south to the Land of the Saxons. He had many sons. He took
2 CONC  possession of lands throughout the Land of the Saxons and made his sons rulers there. Then he went north to the sea and settled on one island. This is where it is now called Odin's Island in Fyon. ”( Odense, Funen Island).
2 CONT
2 CONT Curious phrase:
2 CONT
2 CONT “ And Odin, having learned that Gulvi had good lands in the east, went there, and he and Gulvi ended the matter peacefully, since he judged that he could not cope with Asami. Odin and Asses competed with Gulvi many times in variou
2 CONC s tricks and tricks, and Asses always prevailed. "
2 CONT
2 CONT It turns out that Snorri opposes Odin to the Asam. M. b. One, like Njord, Freyr and Freya was also Van? And what's more:
2 CONT
2 CONT “ It is said as a truth that when Odin and Diy came to the Nordic countries with him, they began to teach people the arts that people have been mastering ever since. One was the most famous of all, and from him people learned all 
2 CONC the arts, for he owned all, although he did not teach everything. "
2 CONT
2 CONT It turns out that Odin was "one of", but the most famous of the dies. Also here it is mentioned for the second time that the Asses came from the southeast in relation to the northern lands, where Odin eventually settled.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Njord. Rules in Uppsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Freyr (Yngwie, hence the Ynglings), Gerd's wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Freya, the last of the gods.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Freya then began to make sacrifices, since she was the only one of the gods to survive , and she then became very famous, so that all noble women, as well as every owner of her property and every mistress who has her property, be
2 CONC gan to be called by her name."
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Fjolnir, son of Yngwie-Freyr. Rules in Uppsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Sveigdir, son of Frey. Wife - Vana from Vani. Rules in Uppsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Vanlandi, son of Sveigdir, wife - Driva. Rules in Uppsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Wiesbur, son of Vanlandi, wife - daughter of Audi Rich.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Domaldi, son of Wiesbourg. Rules in Uppsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Domar, son of Domaldi. Wife - Drott, daughter of King Danpa.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Drott was the sister of King Dan the Proud, after whom Denmark is named."
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Duggvi, son of Domar, the first named king.
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Doug, son of Duggvi.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. Agni, son of Dag. Wife - Skjalf, daughter of the defeated Finn Frosty.
2 CONT
2 CONT 13. Alrek and Eirik, sons of Agni. Dageid is the wife of Alrek, daughter of Dag the Mighty.
2 CONT
2 CONT 14. Yngwie and Alv, sons of Alrec.
2 CONT
2 CONT 15. Hooglake, son of Alva.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Hooglake, it was not the Ynglings who ruled for some time, but the sea kings Khaki and Hagbard. Khaki killed Hooglake in the Battle of Fury Fields.
2 CONT
2 CONT 16. Jorund and Eirik, sons of Yngwie, son of Alrek. Eirik died in the battle against Haki, Haki was also seriously wounded and died. Yorund became king. Rules in Uppsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT 17. Aun, sye Yorunda. Rules in Uppsala. He lived for 170 years donating 9 of his sons to Odin.
2 CONT
2 CONT 18. Egil, son of Aun. Rules in Uppsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT 19. Ottar, son of Egil.
2 CONT
2 CONT 20. Adils, son of Ottar. The wife is Irsa.
2 CONT
2 CONT 21. Eystein, son of Adils.
2 CONT
2 CONT 22, Ingvar. Eystein's son.
2 CONT
2 CONT 23. Onund, Road, son of Ingvar.
2 CONT
2 CONT 24. Ingjald, son of Onund.
2 CONT
2 CONT 25. Olav Lumberjack, son of Ingjald.
2 CONT
2 CONT 26, Halfdan White Bone.
2 CONT
2 CONT 27. Eystein, son of Halfdan White Bone.
2 CONT
2 CONT 28. Halfdan the Generous in Gold and Stingy in Food, the son of Eystein.
2 CONT
2 CONT 29. Goodröd the Magnificent / Hunter, son of Halfdan.
2 CONT
2 CONT 30. Olav is the son of Goodred.
2 CONT
2 CONT 31. Rögnevald the Glorious, son of Olav. http://bogdan-nazar.ru/wordpress/saga-ob-inglingah/ Added by Janet Milburn 11/18/20
2 CONT
