1 CONC  So Harald gathered an army and took over the north and west of Norge in 872 and was acknowledged as the King of Norway. He then married Gyda. He instituted taxes on land and possessions and placed an Earl over each district to co
1 CONC llect taxes, administer justice, and serve the king with 60 warriors in case of war.  Many objected and left for the Faroe Islands, Scottish Islands and Iceland.  Harald, therefore took over the Orkney and Shetland Islands.  He ha
1 CONC d six wives and many sons and when 80 years old became weak and turned the government over to son, Eirik.  He died three years later and is buried in a  mound at Hauge near Haugesand in Ryfylke.
