0 @N6000000003796187741@ NOTE [Geoffrey De Normandie, Gedcom BSJTK Smith Family Tree.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT Note:
1 CONT Name Suffix: Duke of Normandy
1 CONT Ancestral File Number: 9GDD-2H
1 CONT Sources:
1 CONT A. Roots 121E, 243A; Kraentzler 1160, 1443, 1453; RC 162, 166; Coe; Guizot; The Normans and Their Myth (chart) by R.H.C. Davis; Pfafman; WED Stokes;
1 CONT A History of the Vikings by Gwyn Jones; Ashley; Norr, p59.
1 CONT He established the Northmen in France and was the first Duke of Normandy.
1 CONT Count of Rouen. Conquered Normandy. Also known as Hrolf (Gongu-Hrolfr),
1 CONT Rollon, Ganger and Granger Rolf.
1 CONT WED says the area near "Mora, Norway, was the domain of the jarl of More, whose son Hrolf, with his followers...in 911 settled in the district later known as Normandy."
1 CONT Roots: Ganger Rolf, "the Viking (or Rollo), banished from Norway to the
1 CONT Hebrides ca. 876; 890 participated in Viking attack on Bayeux, where Count Berenger of Bayeux was killed, and his daughter Poppa taken, 886, by Rollo (now called Count of Rouen) as his "Danish" wife. Under Treaty of St. Clair, 911
1 CONC , received the Duchy of Normandy from Charles III, "the Simple."
1 CONT Davis: Rollo, ruler of Normandy from 911-931. The dukes of Normandy free
1 CONT married with non-Scandinavians. "Rollo is said to have married the daughter of the Frankish king and to have had his son by the daughter of a Frankish count. That son, William, married the daughter of a Frankish count and had his 
1 CONC son, Richard, by a Breton. None of the dukes' wives came from Scandinavia or England, and by the first half of the 11th century their family connections were typically French." An early historian, Dudo, said Rollo wasDanish.
1 CONT Ashley: Count Rolllo or Rolf the Viking., died 993?
1 CONT Norr: Rollo or Rolf, 1st duke of Normandy 912-917-(927), born about 856. He was of the same Danish origin as the ancestors of the English which his descendants conquered in 1066.
1 CONT
1 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Norwegian Viking settled at mouth of Seine. After fighting many battles, made an agreement with King Charles 'The Simple' - received land in Normandie and 911 became 1st Duc de Normandie and vassel of King.
1 CONT
1 CONT AKARolf Wend-a-Foot.
1 CONT
1 CONT Rollo, the Dane, was a Viking pirate that was banished from Norway by his father; and captured Bayeux in 890. He was given the Name of Robert I at his baptism, and was styled as the "Patrician of Normandy".
1 CONT He aquired his nickname "the Ganger", because he was to big for a horse to carry and had to walk.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was granted land in North western France in 911 by Charles "the Simple", King of France. Charles hoped that Rollo would defend his new land, barring the length of the Seine River to other Viking groups. Rollo remained faithful 
1 CONC to Charles and he and his son quickly expanded the original land grant at the expense of neighboring French lords and guarded it well against Viking rivals.Even before Rollo's grandson Richard took over the domain in 942, the desc
1 CONC endants of the Vikings had accepted Christianity, intermarried with the local population and adopted the French language. Already they were being called Normans,a contraction of Northmen, and the irterritory became known as Norman
1 CONC dy. Richard's (Rollo's grandson) great-grandson was King William I, conqueror of England.
1 CONT
1 CONT Rollo, also called ROLF, or ROU, French ROLLON (b. c. 860--d. c. 932), 
1 CONT Scandinavian rover who founded the duchy of Normandy.
1 CONT Making himself independent of King Harald I of Norway, Rollo sailed off
1 CONT to raid Scotland, England, Flanders, and France on pirating expeditions
1 CONT and, about 911, established himself in an area along the Seine River.
1 CONT Charles III the Simple of France held off his siege of Paris, battled him near Chartres, and negotiated the treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte, giving him the part of Neustria that came to be called Normandy; Rollo in return agreed to
1 CONC  end his brigandage. He gave his son, William I Longsword, governance of the dukedom (927) before his death. Rollo was baptized in 912 but is said to have died a pagan.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dead
0 @N6000000003796223439@ NOTE [Geoffrey De Normandie, Gedcom BSJTK Smith Family Tree.ged]
