0 @N6000000003796223591@ NOTE [Geoffrey De Normandie, Gedcom BSJTK Smith Family Tree.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT Note:
1 CONT Name Suffix: Earl of Orkney
1 CONT
1 CONT The data in this section of royal Norwegian genealogy was compiled by
1 CONT historians, Anders Stilloff, and Ola Robøle Hegge of Norway and presented
1 CONT in chart format by Carl M. Ringen Gunderson. The lineage presented here
1 CONT was given to meas part of my ancestry by genealogist Betty Rockswold,
1 CONT associated with the Valdres Samband Lag organization. When asked about 
1 CONT the research done on the lineage, she said: "It would take a 'volume' to
1 CONT describe the connections to royalty of the Kvåle line." She goes on to 
1 CONT saythat she sent a copy of the material to her skeptic cousin, Herman
1 CONT Nettum, in East Toten who is a noted genealogist. After examination of 
1 CONT the chart, which Betty says she is sure he went over with a 'fine tooth
1 CONT comb' hunting for errors, his only criticism was that,while the lineage
1 CONT was correct, no one knowsthe first name of Earl Thorfinn Sigurdson's
1 CONT wife which was listed as being Ingeborg. It appears that the lineage in
1 CONT this database links to Scandinavian royalty insofar as the genealogy
1 CONT accounts written by the medieval writers is correct. The vice consul of
1 CONT Norway, Lars Løberg, says that the medieval writers, most notably Snorri
1 CONT Sturluson, may have had a political motive for presenting the royal line
1 CONT as an old Norwegian dynasty. Since the lineage in this database ties to
1 CONT the traditionallyaccepted royalty line, it is presented here.)
0 @N6000000003796259385@ NOTE [Geoffrey De Normandie, Gedcom BSJTK Smith Family Tree.ged]
1 CONT
