0 @N6000000003949726314@ NOTE According to medieval historian, Snorii Sturluson, Olav's father, King Harald I (Haarfagre/Fairhair), bestowed the title of "King" to his sons and divided the land between them to rule.
1 CONT He was also called "Olav of Viken" and "Olaf Geirstatha-Alf." The name of his wife is unknown.
1 CONT He took over Westfold in 930 after brother Bjørn was slain by brother Erik. He raised Guthroth Bjørnsson as a foster child.   He had taken over Ranrike in about 900 after brother Guthorm was slain by Solvi Klofi.
1 CONT After his father, King Harald Fairhair, died in 933 and brother Erik "Bloodaxe" took over, he and bother Sigroth agreed to meet the next spring in Tonsberg. Erik summoned a great force and sailed to Tonsberg and killed both Olaf a
1 CONC nd Sigroth in a battle in the hills east of town.
